title DAHL-J11r1 — council loads a sky; the odd fractal gives a tie-free quorum and complete triads
prompt Read REMEMBER + the 1024-round itinerary; take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; open own design rounds, make progress, double-seat visions, send each increment, STOP at custody gates.
think Journey 10 (Membership) closed; REMEMBER + the itinerary name Season 3 Journey 11 (Council skies) as the next Lindy-first crux — loadable topologies, odd-quorum fractal 3-9-15-27, modality roles. A new domain, so the filling law asks a self-approved design read first.
think Grounded in the loadable-topologies brief and comlink/topology.rye: the Sky struct already holds compass_sky (12-5-12, d60) and council_sky (15-3-9, d27). The council sky's four counts are exactly 3-9-15-27 — every one odd — while compass_sky's prosperity is 60, even.
think The crux distinct from J10: J10's quorum was a caller-supplied threshold over a flat roster; J11's quorum is *derived from a loaded sky's odd fractal level*. Because the body is odd, 2*quorum > size, so yes and no can never both reach the majority — a proposal is never left on a tie. The even d60 refuses EvenCouncil; that is why council_sky exists beside the civic sky.
think Modality roles (initiator/sustainer/adapter) are a pure function of seat (seat mod 3), so any triad is complete and the role can never drift from the seated body.
think Wrote the exploration (self-approved), then pond/apps/council_sky.rye: Council.load(sky, size) refuses NotAFractalLevel / EvenCouncil / TooManySeats; vote yes/no per seat, one ballot per seat per proposal (AlreadyVoted), outcome derived from the tally, invariant asserting both sides can never reach quorum. max_seats=64 so the even d60 refuses for being *even*, never merely too large.
